{
  "name": "mobile.de detail page payload capture",
  "capturedBy": "Felix, Proxem AI",
  "capturedOn": "2026-09-08",
  "method": "Captured with Google Chrome for Testing 150 launched manually with --remote-debugging-port and a fresh profile, then driven over CDP. NOT launched by puppeteer.launch: mobile.de serves an Access denied interstitial to a Puppeteer-launched browser, and that difference is the reason an earlier session concluded the content script was not injecting at all. Navigations were paced 9 to 11 seconds apart, the same courtesy Pax used on the tax simulator. UI locale was set by visiting the locale home page first on mobile.de, and by the domain plus path prefix on AutoScout24.",
  "privacy": "Trimmed on capture to the fields the extractor actually reads. Seller identity, contact details, dealer addresses, advert free text and photographs were deliberately never stored. Advert ids and slugs are retained only so a case can be re-checked.",
  "doNotEdit": "Do not edit the captured block. It is measured ground truth. If the site changes shape, capture again and replace the file, do not hand-edit a value to make a test pass. Editing a captured payload to match the parser is the exact fault this file exists to prevent.",
  "whyThisExists": "test/mobilede-extract.mjs describes itself honestly as a realistic mock, because mobile.de is DataDome-walled and nobody had captured a real page. That mock asserts a schema.org Car JSON-LD node which does not appear on any live page sampled, so the whole readJsonLd branch, including the last fallback inside isDetailPage, was only ever exercised against invented data.",
  "coverage": {
    "uiLanguages": [
      "de",
      "en",
      "fr",
      "nl"
    ],
    "detailPaths": [
      "/fahrzeuge/details.html",
      "/nl/voertuigen/details.html"
    ],
    "adverts": 8
  },
  "notCovered": [
    "The French and English detail path nouns are NOT confirmed. /fr/vehicules/details.html and /en/vehicle/details.html both resolved and returned lang=fr and lang=en, but rendered no spec table, so they may not be the real detail paths. The French and English LABEL sets below were captured on the German path with the session locale switched, which is a real rendering the site serves.",
    "Only /fahrzeuge/details.html and /nl/voertuigen/details.html are confirmed detail paths.",
    "All cases are BMW used cars from one search. No new cars beyond the sample, no motorcycles.",
    "8 adverts is a shape sample. It is evidence that a Car JSON-LD node is absent, not proof that it can never appear."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Not one of the 8 adverts carries a schema.org Car, Vehicle or Product JSON-LD node. Every page carries exactly one Organization node and nothing else.",
    "Combined with 4 further adverts inspected on 2026-09-08 before this capture was formalised, 12 distinct live detail pages have now been checked and none carried a Car node.",
    "The spec labels are served in the user's UI language, including on the German path, so the path a user is on does not predict the language of the labels.",
    "The detail path noun is translated per locale: fahrzeuge in German, voertuigen in Dutch."
  ],
